    "created_at": "2018-03-14T05:13:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-14T05:13:03Z",
    "body": "I think we can and should put normative limitations on execCommand; we can't just ignore it, as it's a key part of the web platform---just one we don't have a lot of editor or implementer resources for making better. But keep in mind the HTML Standard says\r\n\r\n> User agents are encouraged to implement the features described in the execCommand specification.\r\n\r\nand normatively gives the IDL for these interfaces. We shouldn't allow sandbox escapes through them on the basis that we're hoping to one day remove them; they need to be secure in the meantime.\r\n\r\nTo fix this bug, we should ideally edit https://w3c.github.io/editing/execCommand.html#execcommand() to include the sandboxing check, and update the list mentioned in the OP. And we should make sure this is tested.\r\n\r\n@fred-wang or @johanneswilm, are you interested in helping with this?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/372906830/reactions",
