    "created_at": "2018-03-14T07:56:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-14T07:56:08Z",
    "body": "Hi all,\r\n\r\nexecCommand(\"print\", ...) is implemented in WebKit and Chromium at least.\r\n\r\nallow-modals has been implemented in Chromium, but initially execCommand(\"print\", ...) had been forgotten: \r\nhttps://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=483624\r\nhttps://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=658985\r\n\r\nFor WebKit, allow-modals was implemented (for execCommand print too) in\r\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=171321\r\n\r\nI finally merged the WPT tests to check that modals are blocked:\r\nhttps://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/pull/6618\r\nI removed the test for execCommand(\"print\", ...) for now (it is easy to add though) and checking the cases when modals are *not* blocked seemed a bit complicated with WPT when I tried. All of these cases are verified in Chromium & WebKit's test suites, though.\r\n\r\nI don't plan to work on standardization but might still help with Chromium/WebKit/Mozilla's implementation/removal/stats if necessary (AFAIK we don't have usage stats). However, I have to say for now it's not my main work focus, I was just opening it for the record and because @ayg asked me to do so.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
